hadiths[34]{hadithnumber,text}:
"506","Syedna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned the tribe of Daws. He said: Those people—and he mentioned their men and women. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his hands. That man said: «انا لله وانا اليه راجعون» , By the Lord of the Ka'bah! The people of Daws are destroyed. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his hands and said: ""O Allah! Grant guidance to the people of Daws."""
"507","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked a horse of the ""shikal"" type (shikal: a horse whose right leg and left forearm are white)."
"508","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves after me, but do not take my kunyah."" He narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked a horse that had whiteness on its right leg and left forearm."
"509","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah guarantees the person who goes out in His path for jihad, believing in Allah and affirming His messengers, that Allah will admit him to Paradise, or if He returns him, He will return him with reward and spoils of war. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color of blood, but its fragrance will be the fragrance of musk. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! If I did not find it hard upon the Muslims, I would never stay behind any expedition fighting in the path of Allah, but I do not find the means to provide them with mounts, nor do they find the means, and it is hard upon them that they do not go out with me. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! I wish that I fight in the path of Allah and am martyred, then fight and am martyred, then fight and am martyred."""
"510","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us, in which he mentioned betrayal and explained its severity, saying: ""O people! I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he has taken a camel and it is groaning, and he says: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I cannot do anything for you before Allah; I have conveyed the commands to you. I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he comes carrying a goat and it is bleating, and that person says: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I cannot do anything for you before Allah; I have conveyed the commands to you. I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he has taken a horse and it is neighing, and that person says: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I cannot do anything for you before Allah; I have conveyed the commands to you. I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he has taken a soul and it is screaming, and that person will say: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I cannot do anything for you before Allah; I have conveyed the commands to you. I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he has taken a piece of cloth and it is moving, and that person says: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I cannot do anything for you before Allah; I have conveyed the commands to you. I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he has taken gold or silver and he says: O Messenger of Allah! Help me, and I will say: I cannot do anything for you before Allah; I have conveyed the commands to you."""
"511","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight the Jews, until the stone behind which a Jew is hiding will say, 'O Muslim! There is a Jew behind me, so kill him.'"""
"512","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no deity except Allah, establish prayer, and pay zakat. When they do so, their blood and wealth become forbidden (to be harmed) except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning is with Allah."""
"513","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no deity except Allah."""
"514","Abdullah bin Rabah narrated: We went to (visit) Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) was also present with us. One of us would arrange food each day; when it was my turn, they all gathered at my place, but the food was not yet ready. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: ""Abu Hurairah! Call the Ansar to me."" I called them, and they came running. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to them: ""O group of Ansar! Do you see the scattered people of Quraysh? When you encounter them tomorrow, cut them down."" Hammad (the narrator) gestured with his right hand over his left hand and said (cut them like this). ""Then you are to meet me at Safa (hill)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed Khalid bin Walid (may Allah be pleased with him) to the right flank, Zubair bin Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him) to the left flank, and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him) to the infantry in the valley. The narrator said: When the next day came, we encountered them, and whoever of them we saw, we put him to (the sleep of) death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) conquered Makkah and ascended the hill of Safa. The Ansar came and surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at Safa. Abu Sufyan came and said: O Messenger of Allah! The great groups of Quraysh have perished; after today, Quraysh will remain no more. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters his house is safe; whoever lays down his arms is safe; whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is also safe; and whoever closes his door is also safe."" The Ansar said: As for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he has felt compassion for his people and has developed longing and desire for his homeland. Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him); when that state ended, he said: ""O group of Ansar! Did you say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has felt compassion for his people and has developed longing and desire for his homeland? Then what is my name? I am Allah's servant and His Messenger. I migrated to Allah and to you; my living and dying is with you."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! We only said this because of our special relationship with Allah and His Messenger. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah and His Messenger affirm you and accept your excuse."""
"515","Sulaiman bin Mughira narrated regarding this hadith: The Prophet (peace be upon him) appointed Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him) over such a foot army that did not have armor."
"516","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the first three people about whom judgment will be passed will be: a martyr, he will be brought before Allah, He will remind him of His blessings, and he will recognize them. He (Allah) will say: What did you do about them? He will say: I fought in Your cause until I was martyred. He (Allah) will say: You have lied, you fought so that it would be said: He is brave, and so it was said. Then He will command regarding him, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into the Fire. Another man will be brought who acquired knowledge and taught it, and recited the Qur'an. He will remind him of His blessings, and he will recognize them. He (Allah) will say: What did you do about them? He will say: I acquired knowledge, taught it for Your sake, and recited the Qur'an. He (Allah) will say: You have lied, you acquired knowledge so that it would be said: So-and-so is a scholar, so-and-so is a reciter, and so it was said. Then He will command regarding him, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into the Fire. Then a man will be brought to whom Allah had given all kinds of wealth. He will remind him of His blessings, and he will recognize them. He (Allah) will say: What did you do about them? He will say: I did not leave any path or place where You like spending, except that I spent there. He (Allah) will say: You have lied, you did so that it would be said: He is generous, and so it was said. Then He will command regarding him, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into the Fire."""
"517","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said in the explanation of Allah’s statement: “You are the best nation brought forth for mankind,”: We will bring them in chains and we will admit them (into Islam)."
"518","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from the expedition of Tabuk and his mount was ahead of him, suddenly a Bedouin passed by with a fat, strong camel, reciting rajaz poetry, and the Prophet’s mount trembled. A man said: If his energy and strength were in the way of Allah, and if he is returned to his family, then he is in the way of Allah. (Upon hearing this) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “If his energy and strength are returned to his parents so that he may serve and suffice them, then he is in the way of Allah, and if he is returned to his family, then he is in the way of Allah, and if his intention is mutual boasting and increasing wealth, then he is in the way of Taghut (falsehood).”"
"519","With the same chain of narration, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Allah! Spending a morning or an evening in the way of Allah is better than the world and whatever is in it."""
"520","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The truly deprived one is he who was deprived from the distribution of the spoils of Banu Kalb."""
"521","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever receives a wound in the way of Allah, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with its color like the color of blood, while its fragrance will be that of musk."""
"522","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah is extremely angry with the person whom the Messenger of Allah has killed, and Allah is also extremely angry with the person who adopts the name 'King of Kings' (Shahanshah); there is no king except Allah."""
"523","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Rifaa’ah bin Zaid Al-Judhami (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a slave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he set out with him towards Khaybar. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from Khaybar, he stayed in the valley of ‘Ashiyyah between ‘Asr and Maghrib. That slave stood up and began to unload the saddle from the riding animal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when suddenly an arrow came from an unknown direction and struck him, and he was killed. We said: “Congratulations to you for Paradise!” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Never! By the One in Whose hand is my soul! The cloak which he stole from the spoils of the Muslims at the time of the battle of Khaybar is now burning upon him as a flame of fire.” The narrator said: One of your companions came in a state of fear and said: “O Messenger of Allah! I had picked up two straps of shoes.” So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “For both of them, two similar things will be prepared for you in Hell.”"
"524","Sayyida Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh bin 'Afra' (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We used to participate in battles with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and we would give water to (the fighters) and serve them, and we would transport the martyrs and the wounded to Madinah."
"525","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him), a woman told him, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slept, then woke up smiling. She asked: O Messenger of Allah! Did you laugh because of me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No, rather because of some people from my Ummah who will undertake a naval expedition; their example is like that of kings on thrones."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then slept again, then woke up smiling and said: ""Some people from my Ummah will set out for a naval expedition; they will receive little spoils of war but they will be forgiven."" She asked: O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah that He includes me among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for her. The narrator said: Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us that the woman participated in the expedition of Al-Mundhir bin Zubair, which was towards the land of Rome; she was with them and she passed away in the land of Rome."
"526","Lady Umm Haram bint Milhan (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slept, then woke up; the narrator mentioned it in a similar manner."
"527","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever ties a horse in the way of Allah (for jihad), and spends on it with the intention of reward, then its being full, its being hungry, its being thirsty, its being quenched, and its urination and defecation will all be in his scale (of deeds) on the Day of Judgment."""
"528","Sayyida Umm Atiyya (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We used to participate in battles along with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). I participated in seven battles with him; I used to stay in their tents, prepare food for them, and treat the wounded."
"529","Lady Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We participated in seven battles with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I used to prepare food for them (the fighters), take care of the sick, and treat the wounded."
"530","Sayyida Umm Waraqah bint Abdullah bin Harith Ansariyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: She had memorized the Qur'an. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was about to go for the Battle of Badr, she said to him: ""Do you permit me to go with you? I will treat and nurse your wounded and sick, perhaps Allah will grant me martyrdom."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has written martyrdom for you."" Thus, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to call her 'the martyr' and he ordered her to lead her household in prayer. She had a mu'adhdhin (caller to prayer), and she continued to lead her household in prayer until her slave girl and her slave strangled her. She had told both of them that after her death they would be free. Both of them killed her during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). It became well known that Umm Waraqah had been killed, and that her slave and slave girl had killed her. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) announced among the people: ""Umm Waraqah's slave girl and her slave strangled her and killed her, and both have fled."" They were brought and crucified, and they were the first to be executed in Madinah. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke the truth. He used to say: 'Come with us, we will meet the martyr.'"""
"531","The daughter of Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: During the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), my father participated in a battle, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to take care of us regarding the milking of our goat. He would milk the goat into a vessel and it would become full. Then when Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) returned (from the battle), he would milk it, and its milk returned (became less)."
"532","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was helped by the east wind, while the people of 'Ad were destroyed by the west wind."""
"533","Hazrat Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) narrated a hadith similar to the previous one."
"534","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Najdah Haruri wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) in which he asked about killing children, at what age the rulings of orphanhood end for a child, about women—whether they will participate in fighting and jihad, about khums, and about slaves—whether they have a share in the spoils of war. (Regarding these matters) he asked: So he wrote a letter to me, as for children, if you are Khidr (peace be upon him), then you will be able to distinguish between a believer and a disbeliever, so kill him; as for a child, when he reaches puberty, the rulings of orphanhood end for him; as for women, they used to go out with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for fighting, they would treat the sick, take care of the wounded, and participate in fighting; as for khums, we said: it is our right, but our people did not accept this from us; as for the slave, he used to be given a share from the spoils of war."
"535","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he mentioned some people whom Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) had burned, so he said: If I had been there, I would not have burned them, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not punish anyone with Allah's punishment (i.e., fire)."" And I would certainly have killed them, and also because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever changes his religion, kill him."""
"536","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever did this and that, then the young men hastened towards it, and the elders (those of greater age) remained steadfast under the banners. When Allah granted them victory, the young men came and began to demand what had been assigned for them, and the elders said: We were your helpers and we were under the banners. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse: 'They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils of war belong to Allah and the Messenger. So fear Allah and set matters right among yourselves.'"""
"537","Ikrimah narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) a similar narration, and he reported this addition: We were your supporters; if you have become prominent, it is for our sake that you have become prominent."
"538","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said on the occasion of the Battle of Badr: ""Whoever accomplishes this feat, for him there will be this reward."" So the young men went forth, while the elders remained stationed under the banners. When Allah granted them victory, the young men came and began to demand the spoils of war, while the elders said: We were under the banners and we were your supporters; if you had been defeated, then you would not have given us preference. So Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: ""They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils of war are for Allah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited (from the beginning of Surah Al-Anfal) until he reached: ""Just as Allah brought you out of your home with the truth, while a group of the believers disliked it."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) distributed the spoils of war equally among them."
"539","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that on the day of the Battle of Badr, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in a tent, he said: ""O Allah! I ask You by Your covenant and Your promise."" Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! You have supplicated to your Lord with great persistence. Then he (the Prophet) came out (of the tent), and was saying: ""To Him belongs greatness in the heavens. Rather, the appointed time for them is the Day of Resurrection, and the Day of Resurrection is a great calamity and a very distressing thing."""
